    "result_text": "The only test class in the repo is `AcceptanceTest` (with its supporting base/helper), and both its tests pass along with a full `BUILD SUCCESS`.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `ownerSegment` derived field (`<TIER>_<AREA>`) following the existing patterns for computed owner fields (`locality`, `timezone`, `membershipLevel`, etc.), keeping each piece of logic in a small, single-responsibility unit:\n\n- **`CityRegions.isKnownRegion(String)`** \u2014 added the canonical known-region test (NSW/VIC/QLD) to the class that already owns the region/`UNKNOWN` concept, derived from its existing lookup table so there's one source of truth.\n- **`OwnerSegment`** (new model helper) \u2014 formats the segment from a membership level and locality: `PREMIUM` when level \u2265 3 else `STANDARD`; `METRO` when the locality is a known region else `REGIONAL`. Mirrors the style of sibling helpers like `RegionTimezones`.\n- **`Owner.getOwnerSegment()`** \u2014 a `@Transient` getter that composes the existing `getMembershipLevel()` and `getLocality()` derivations through `OwnerSegment`, reusing rather than duplicating logic.\n- **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the read-only `ownerSegment` property (enum of the four values) to the `Owner` schema, so the OpenAPI-generated `OwnerDto` gains the field and MapStruct maps it by name automatically into the `GET /api/owners/{id}` response.\n\nBoth acceptance tests (`STANDARD_METRO` for a known NSW city, `STANDARD_REGIONAL` for an unknown city) pass, and the full suite is green.",
